check-ntl.c is a copy of:
https://maths-people.anu.edu.au/~brent/ftp/trinom/check-ntl.c
linked to at
https://maths-people.anu.edu.au/~brent/trinom.html

It is included here for convenience.


check-ntl.c dates from 2013 or earlier.
It is a short file that contains no copyright or licensing information,
but since it is incorporated in Richard Brent's academic webpage
and served from an FTP subdirectory there,
it was presumably written by him.

Since it has different authorship, for copyright purposes
it is not necessarily covered by the same license terms
as the other files in this Git repository,
which are licensed under GPL v3 (or later).

check-ntl uses and links to the NTL library.
The NTL library uses the GMP library,
and for performance reasons,
the NTL library file that is used for linking
should be one that was compiled with
./configure NTL_GF2X_LIB=on
which uses the GF2X library

The NTL library is licensed under LGPL v2.1 (or later)
The GMP library is licensed under either LGPL v3 or GPL v2 (or later)
The GF2X library has complicated licensing terms.
It is licensed under either GPL v3 or LGPL v2.1 (or later),
however the applicable license is not at the discretion of the user,
but rather depends on the exact circumstances of its use.
The apps/ subdir of the GF2X library is licensed under GPL v2 (or later)
The GF2X library was written by Richard Brent, Pierrick Gaudry, Emmanuel Thomé, Paul Zimmermann





verify_gf2x_trinomial.py was written for this project by Claude AI in July 2026
and for copyright purposes it has the same authorship and same GPL license
as the other files in this Git repository.

It is a much slower implementation of the same thing that check-ntl does,
and serves as a double-check, since it is algorithmically simpler and relies
only on the GMP library and not on NTL or GF2X.
